-- title:
--   Collapse of K(̄ j(q),̄ j(q^{Nℓ})) under separability
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $N$ be a positive natural number, let $\ell$ be a prime and assume $K$ has characteristic $\ell$. Work inside the field of Laurent series `LaurentSeries K`, and write $\bar j(q)$ for `jqModC K`, the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the power series obtained from $E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-24}$-type integral data `jNum` by reducing its integer coefficients into $K$ — that is, the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant read in $K$. For $M\ge 1$, `jqNModC K M` is the image of $\bar j(q)$ under the ring homomorphism `qExpand K M` that multiplies all Laurent exponents by $M$, i.e. the substitution $q\mapsto q^M$, so `jqNModC K M` $=\bar j(q^M)$; and `modularFunctionFieldC K M` is the intermediate field $K(\bar j(q),\bar j(q^M))$ of $K\subseteq K((q))$ generated by these two series. The hypothesis is that $\bar j(q^N)$ is a separable element over the intermediate field $K(\bar j(q))$ generated by $\bar j(q)$ alone (in particular that it is algebraic over it). The conclusion is the equality of intermediate fields $K(\bar j(q),\bar j(q^{N\ell}))=K(\bar j(q),\bar j(q^{N}))$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$\ell$ degeneration statement that adjoining the level-$N\ell$ expansion $\bar j(q^{N\ell})$ adds nothing beyond level $N$, conditional on separability of $\bar j(q^N)$ over $K(\bar j(q))$; separability itself is a property of the level-$N$ modular polynomial and is assumed rather than proved here. It is used in the project's treatment of separability for modular polynomial families, via [`ModularCurve.isSeparable_jqNModC_of_modularPolynomialFamily`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isSeparable_jqNModC_of_modularPolynomialFamily).
